        "original_id": "9f20cbf9-cd69-5d86-9e27-9297e8d2e8cb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: The Attack, Marmalade, The Nice, Andromeda, Atomic Rooster\n- People: Richard Shirman, Alan Whitehead, David O'List, John Du Cann, Jeff Beck\n- Topics: freakbeat, psychedelic rock, \"Hi Ho Silver Lining\"\n\nFacts:\n- Jeff Beck, born Geoffrey Arnold Beck on 24 June 1944, is an English rock guitarist.\n- The Attack were a freakbeat and psychedelic rock band formed in 1966 around singer Richard Shirman, who was born on 26 April 1949 in London and died in July 2017.\n- The first lineup of The Attack featured drummer Alan Whitehead from Marmalade, guitarist David O'List, who was later of The Nice, and John Du Cann, who was later of Andromeda and Atomic Rooster.\n- The Attack released a version of \"Hi Ho Silver Lining\" a few days earlier than Jeff Beck.",
